From fa9eebf11cb934d45e0532797c950ffb221b5627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:52:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mac: turn a 360 view by the trackpad's gestures in the VO

A script turning a view by the gestures (view360) applies them through
--glsl-shader-opts, which waits for the VO: at 60 Hz the gestures came
faster than it could set them and the view fell behind, by seconds
while playing. Now each gesture message carries a number, the script
says which one its values include (afp_input_seq), and the VO, before
it draws, turns the view (view360_yaw, _pitch, _roll, _fov) by the
gestures after it with the same geometry near the picture's middle,
and is woken to draw as each comes in, playing or paused. The script
stays the one that turns the view exactly (what's under the mouse
staying under it); the VO only bridges the frames until its values
come. The little planet's pan is left to the script.

--macos-latency-test's timer now runs from MacCommon, stopped when the
VO goes: polled from the view, it could read the options after they
were freed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
